IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part III: capacity and powers (s 15 to s 18).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. What a corporation can do, what it may not do, what is not undone by
-- breaking its own rules, and what it cannot say against a person who dealt with it.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Each rule is named `<what it decides> within s <section>`. Where the Act says a
-- thing is "not necessary", "not invalid" or "not deemed" "by reason only" of something, the rule takes
-- both the something and the other ground as facts, and the something changes nothing: the tests assert
-- that.

§ `Part III -- Capacity and powers`

§§ `s 15 capacity of a corporation`

-- s 15(1): "the capacity and, subject to this Act, the rights, powers and privileges of a natural person".
-- The input is the one thing that can take a right away: a provision of this Act that does.
-- src:216 | 15 (1) A corporation has the capacity and, subject to this Act, the rights, powers and privileges of a natural person.
@ref CBCA s 15(1) capacity of a corporation (src:216)
GIVEN `the body is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of this Act takes the right, power or privilege away from the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the rest of this Act (pieces cb2 to cb5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has the right, power or privilege of a natural person within s 15(1)` MEANS
        `the body is a corporation`
    AND (NOT `a provision of this Act takes the right, power or privilege away from the corporation`)

-- src:218 | (2) A corporation may carry on business throughout Canada.
@ref CBCA s 15(2) idem (src:218)
GIVEN `the body is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may carry on business throughout Canada within s 15(2)` MEANS
    `the body is a corporation`

-- src:220 | (3) A corporation has the capacity to carry on its business, conduct its affairs and exercise its powers in any jurisdiction outside Canada to the extent that the laws of such jurisdiction permit.
@ref CBCA s 15(3) extra-territorial capacity (src:220)
GIVEN `the body is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws of the jurisdiction outside Canada permit it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has the capacity to act in the jurisdiction outside Canada within s 15(3)` MEANS
        `the body is a corporation`
    AND `the laws of the jurisdiction outside Canada permit it`

§§ `s 16 powers of a corporation`

-- s 16(1): "It is not necessary for a by-law to be passed in order to confer any particular power on the
-- corporation or its directors." The power comes from somewhere else (this Act, the articles); the rule
-- takes that as a fact, and whether a by-law was passed changes nothing.
-- src:222 | 16 (1) It is not necessary for a by-law to be passed in order to confer any particular power on the corporation or its directors.
@ref CBCA s 16(1) powers of a corporation (src:222)
GIVEN `the power is otherwise conferred on the corporation or its directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a by-law has been passed to confer the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation or its directors have the power within s 16(1)` MEANS
    `the power is otherwise conferred on the corporation or its directors`

-- s 16(2): "shall not carry on any business or exercise any power that it is restricted by its articles
-- from carrying on or exercising, nor shall the corporation exercise any of its powers in a manner
-- contrary to its articles".
-- src:224 | (2) A corporation shall not carry on any business or exercise any power that it is restricted by its articles from carrying on or exercising, nor shall the corporation exercise any of its powers in a manner contrary to its articles.
@ref CBCA s 16(2) restricted business or powers (src:224)
GIVEN `the articles restrict the corporation from carrying on the business or exercising the power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation would exercise the power in a manner contrary to its articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is forbidden to carry on the business or exercise the power within s 16(2)` MEANS
        `the articles restrict the corporation from carrying on the business or exercising the power`
    OR  `the corporation would exercise the power in a manner contrary to its articles`

-- s 16(3): "No act of a corporation, including any transfer of property to or by a corporation, is invalid
-- by reason only that the act or transfer is contrary to its articles or this Act." An act can still be
-- invalid on another ground, and the rule says so by taking that ground as the only thing that decides.
-- src:226 | (3) No act of a corporation, including any transfer of property to or by a corporation, is invalid by reason only that the act or transfer is contrary to its articles or this Act.
@ref CBCA s 16(3) rights preserved (src:226)
GIVEN `the act is contrary to the articles of the corporation or to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is invalid on a ground other than that it is contrary to the articles or this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the act of the corporation is invalid within s 16(3)` MEANS
    `the act is invalid on a ground other than that it is contrary to the articles or this Act`

§§ `s 17 no constructive notice`

-- src:228 | 17 No person is affected by or is deemed to have notice or knowledge of the contents of a document concerning a corporation by reason only that the document has been filed by the Director or is available for inspection at an office of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 17 no constructive notice (src:228)
GIVEN `the document has been filed by the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is available for inspection at an office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is otherwise affected by or has notice or knowledge of the contents of the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is affected by or deemed to have notice of the contents of the document within s 17` MEANS
    `the person is otherwise affected by or has notice or knowledge of the contents of the document`

§§ `s 18 authority of directors, officers and agents`

-- The six assertions s 18(1) bars the corporation and a guarantor from making, in the text's order.
-- src:230 | 18 (1) No corporation and no guarantor of an obligation of a corporation may assert against a person dealing with the corporation or against a person who acquired rights from the corporation that
-- src:231 | (a) the articles, by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement have not been complied with;
-- src:232 | (b) the persons named in the most recent notice sent to the Director under section 106 or 113 are not the directors of the corporation;
-- src:233 | (c) the place named in the most recent notice sent to the Director under section 19 is not the registered office of the corporation;
-- src:234 | (d) a person held out by a corporation as a director, officer, agent or mandatary of the corporation has not been duly appointed or has no authority to exercise the powers and perform the duties that are customary in the business of the corporation or usual for a director, officer, agent or mandatary;
-- src:235 | (e) a document issued by any director, officer, agent or mandatary of a corporation with actual or usual authority to issue the document is not valid or genuine; or
-- src:236 | (f) a sale, lease or exchange of property referred to in subsection 189(3) was not authorized.
@ref CBCA s 18(1) authority of directors, officers and agents (src:230-236)
DECLARE `Assertion barred by s 18(1)` IS ONE OF
    `the articles, by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement have not been complied with`
    `the persons named in the most recent notice sent to the Director under section 106 or 113 are not the directors of the corporation`
    `the place named in the most recent notice sent to the Director under section 19 is not the registered office of the corporation`
    `a person held out by the corporation as a director, officer, agent or mandatary has not been duly appointed or has no authority to exercise the customary or usual powers and duties`
    `a document issued by a director, officer, agent or mandatary with actual or usual authority to issue it is not valid or genuine`
    `a sale, lease or exchange of property referred to in subsection 189(3) was not authorized`
    `any other assertion`

-- s 18(2): the bar does not reach "a person who has, or ought to have, knowledge of a situation described
-- in that subsection by virtue of their relationship to the corporation".
-- src:230 | 18 (1) No corporation and no guarantor of an obligation of a corporation may assert against a person dealing with the corporation or against a person who acquired rights from the corporation that
-- src:231 | (a) the articles, by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement have not been complied with;
-- src:232 | (b) the persons named in the most recent notice sent to the Director under section 106 or 113 are not the directors of the corporation;
-- src:233 | (c) the place named in the most recent notice sent to the Director under section 19 is not the registered office of the corporation;
-- src:234 | (d) a person held out by a corporation as a director, officer, agent or mandatary of the corporation has not been duly appointed or has no authority to exercise the powers and perform the duties that are customary in the business of the corporation or usual for a director, officer, agent or mandatary;
-- src:235 | (e) a document issued by any director, officer, agent or mandatary of a corporation with actual or usual authority to issue the document is not valid or genuine; or
-- src:236 | (f) a sale, lease or exchange of property referred to in subsection 189(3) was not authorized.
-- src:238 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of a person who has, or ought to have, knowledge of a situation described in that subsection by virtue of their relationship to the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 18(1), s 18(2) authority of directors, officers and agents (src:230-236 src:238)
GIVEN assertion IS AN `Assertion barred by s 18(1)`
      `the one asserting is the corporation or a guarantor of an obligation of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deals with the corporation or acquired rights from the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has, or ought to have, knowledge of the situation by virtue of their relationship to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the assertion is barred against the person within s 18` MEANS
        `the one asserting is the corporation or a guarantor of an obligation of the corporation`
    AND `the person deals with the corporation or acquired rights from the corporation`
    AND (NOT `the person has, or ought to have, knowledge of the situation by virtue of their relationship to the corporation`)
    AND CONSIDER assertion
        WHEN `the articles, by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement have not been complied with` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the persons named in the most recent notice sent to the Director under section 106 or 113 are not the directors of the corporation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the place named in the most recent notice sent to the Director under section 19 is not the registered office of the corporation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a person held out by the corporation as a director, officer, agent or mandatary has not been duly appointed or has no authority to exercise the customary or usual powers and duties` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a document issued by a director, officer, agent or mandatary with actual or usual authority to issue it is not valid or genuine` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a sale, lease or exchange of property referred to in subsection 189(3) was not authorized` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `any other assertion` THEN FALSE
